            <ArticleTitle>[A Case of Signet-Ring Cell Carcinoma of the Sigmoid Colon with Disseminated Carcinomatosis Successfully Treated with CPT-11/Panitumumab].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2477-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 70-year-old man, who had undergone S-1/oxaliplatin/bevacizumab combination chemotherapy for LNs metastasis of signet-ring cell carcinoma of the sigmoid colon, complained of back pain and lumbago.He was diagnosed with disseminated carcinomatosis of the bone marrow and disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC). He was treated with systemic chemotherapy consisting of CPT-11/panitumumab. After 2 courses of the treatment, the DIC resolved and the back pain and lumbago improved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
